{"slug":"ops-adding-a-domain","title":"Adding a domain","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"callout","tone":"info","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Why Caddy terminates TLS (not Phoenix):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Caddy auto-issues and renews Let's Encrypt certs while Phoenix keeps serving plain HTTP on loopback; Phoenix-native TLS ("},{"type":"text","value":"Plug.SSL","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + cowboy) was deliberately rejected — terminate at the edge and forward "},{"type":"text","value":"X-Forwarded-Proto","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b2","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Stub: "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark.dev","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" DNS does not exist yet. Follow once a domain points at "},{"type":"text","value":"89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b3","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 1 — DNS"},{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" records for apex + "},{"type":"text","value":"www","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → "},{"type":"text","value":"89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (TTL 300). Verify: "},{"type":"text","value":"dig +short your-domain.example","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b5","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 2 — Caddy config"},{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace the "},{"type":"text","value":":80 { reverse_proxy localhost:4000 }","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" block in "},{"type":"text","value":"/etc/caddy/Caddyfile","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"id":"b7","type":"code","value":"your-domain.example, www.your-domain.example {\n    encode zstd gzip\n    reverse_proxy localhost:4000\n\n    header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\"\n    header X-Content-Type-Options \"nosniff\"\n    header Referrer-Policy \"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"\n}"},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Then "},{"type":"text","value":"caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile && systemctl reload caddy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b9","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 3 — Phoenix env"},{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"In "},{"type":"text","value":"/opt/barkpark/.env","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"text","value":"PHX_SCHEME=https","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"PHX_HOST=your-domain.example","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Then "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl restart barkpark.service","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b11","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 4 — Let's Encrypt"},{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Auto-issued/renewed by Caddy on first HTTPS request. Watch: "},{"type":"text","value":"journalctl -u caddy -f | grep -i certificate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 5 — Firewall"},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"sudo ufw delete allow 4000/tcp","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" so Caddy is the only ingress. Verify the bare "},{"type":"text","value":":4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" port times out and HTTPS still serves."}]},{"id":"b15","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 6 — force_ssl stays OFF (not a cutover step)"},{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"api/config/prod.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" keeps "},{"type":"text","value":"force_ssl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" commented out "},{"type":"text","value":"by standing decision","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Golden Rule #5 / Past Mistake #5 — and its Sobelow "},{"type":"text","value":"Config.HTTPS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" row is justified-baselined against "},{"type":"text","value":"config/prod.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"text","value":"api/.sobelow-skips","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (task-f76e9b7b). Caddy already redirects "},{"type":"text","value":":80 → :443","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", so a Phoenix-side redirect buys nothing. "},{"type":"text","value":"Finish the cutover at Step 5 and stop here.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Turning it on is a separate, owner-sign-off change. All four must hold first: (1) "},{"type":"text","value":"curl -sI https://your-domain.example/api/schemas","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"text","value":"200","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — TLS live. (2) "},{"type":"text","value":"curl -sI http://your-domain.example/api/schemas","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"text","value":"30x","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"text","value":"https://","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Caddy, not Phoenix, owns the redirect. (3) No bare-HTTP ingress is left: the 7-day "},{"type":"text","value":"http://89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" block under Pitfalls is a "},{"type":"text","value":"blocker","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"text","value":"force_ssl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" would 301 it to "},{"type":"text","value":"https://89.167.28.206","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", which has no certificate. (4) The Sobelow baseline row is re-fingerprinted in the same PR, or the security gate reds."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Only then uncomment the block "},{"type":"text","value":"prod.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" already carries. "},{"type":"text","value":"rewrite_on: [:x_forwarded_proto]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is mandatory — without it Phoenix sees "},{"type":"text","value":"http","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and redirects forever. Skip "},{"type":"text","value":"hsts: true","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; Caddy emits HSTS at Step 2. Then "},{"type":"text","value":"make rebuild","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b19","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 7 — Smoke test"},{"id":"b20","type":"code","value":"curl -I https://your-domain.example/api/schemas    # expect 200 (public)\ncurl -sL \"https://your-domain.example/v1/data/query/production/post?perspective=published\""},{"id":"b21","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Pitfalls (from the 2026 api.barkpark.cloud cutover)"},{"id":"b22","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"HSTS: do NOT add ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"preload","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — preload is hard to undo. "},{"type":"text","value":"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is the ceiling."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Let's Encrypt rate limit: 5 duplicate certs per 7 days.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Past 5, issuance fails — wait it out or use the staging CA ("},{"type":"text","value":"acme_ca https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}],[{"type":"text","value":"7-day bare-IP grace window.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Keep a transitional "},{"type":"text","value":"http://89.167.28.206 { reverse_proxy localhost:4000 }","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" block at least 7 days post-cutover; remove only at zero bare-IP traffic. ACME HTTP-01 issuance "},{"type":"text","value":"and renewal","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" need port 80 — keep the HTTP path until one renewal completes (~30–60 days)."}]]},{"id":"b23","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Rollback (two tiers)"},{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshot first — the mandatory rollback anchor: "},{"type":"text","value":"sudo cp -a /etc/caddy/Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.pre-tls-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)","marks":["code"]}]},{"id":"b25","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Tier 1 — revert Caddyfile (~30 s):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" restore snapshot, "},{"type":"text","value":"caddy validate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl reload caddy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (graceful; "},{"type":"text","value":"restart","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" only if reload fails — it drops in-flight connections)."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Tier 2 — nuclear (Caddy wedged):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl stop caddy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", restore snapshot, "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl start caddy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", check "},{"type":"text","value":"systemctl status caddy","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]},{"id":"b26","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Related"},{"id":"b27","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"web/README.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — Vercel demo; mixed-content caveat disappears after this TLS work."}],[{"type":"text","value":"CLAUDE.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — never enable "},{"type":"text","value":"force_ssl","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" without verified "},{"type":"text","value":"X-Forwarded-Proto","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" trust."}]]}],"related":[]}
